  "_comment": "`eic.pilot -> 20,21,22` (plan/BENCHMARK_DESIGN.md \u00a73), the ablation arm against `eic.19`. Same corpus, same assay order (D14) and same biosample split as configs/regime.equiv.json; the only differences are the training slice and the eval chromosomes. Transferable parameters are fit on the 44 ENCODE Pilot Regions lifted to hg38 (`regions`, D32), minus the four that fall on the eval chromosomes \u2014 those are cut by `train_chroms`, not by the BED, so the BED stays correct for any other split. ALL 44 Pilot Regions are kept, chrX included: ENm006 and ENr324 sit on chrX and are 7.16 % of the training scope (1,832,771 of 25,588,197 bp). `eic.19` has no chrX at all, so the two regimes differ in chrX presence as well as in slice; that is accepted and disclosed, not fixed. Training scope: 40 regions, 25,588,197 bp, 1,023,489 contained 25 bp bins (a containment count \u2014 25,588,197 is not divisible by 25). Departures from regime.equiv.json besides the split: seed 42 (the default every other config uses; equiv's 0 reproduced an old bake) and kinds without `pval` (D24 builds it last). `eval_pairs` is DECLARED here (D31), 38 pairs generated by tools/declare_eval_pairs.py from the store manifest sha256 c9a95e4e424d94496be7197ad4aa3d08cd9d7d31144bcf72f53ca50505a2fd83 (re-derived unchanged after t78's DNase promotion; it was declared against 6c0e0c3e371383eaa75a078e663ee6593af127cc96241dc53e9e26d4c7c89397, and the pairing is a function of biosample names alone, which the promotion did not touch); the input is the T_ prompt cell and the target is the truth cell, which is what restores the V_ panel to 45 scoreable experiments (26 V_ + 12 B_ pairs).",
